    <string name="tutorial_group">Tutorial</string>
    <string name="tutorial_providers">Custom providers</string>
    <string name="tutorial_providers_desc">How to add a Blog or a novel website</string>
    <string name="tutorial_providers_body">1. Open Settings → Custom providers → Add provider.\n\n2. Choose the type:\n• Blog — for Blogger/Blogspot (e.g. myblog.blogspot.com). If the blog has a “Lista de Novelas”, each novel is listed one by one with its full chapter list.\n• Website — for Madara / WordPress novel sites. Only name and URL are needed.\n\n3. Wait for the check. When it succeeds, the provider appears in Search and in Providers.\n\n4. Use Manage providers to edit or delete. Advanced lets you set CSS selectors by hand if auto-setup fails.\n\nTip: for Spanish blogs, prefer type Blog. The word “the” often finds nothing; the app tests with empty / Spanish words for blogs.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_download">Downloads</string>
    <string name="tutorial_download_desc">How to download novels and choose the format</string>
    <string name="tutorial_download_body">1. Open a novel → Download.\n\n2. You can download all chapters or a range (e.g. 1-10, 15).\n\n3. Chapters per file: leave empty for one EPUB with everything, or set a number (e.g. 50) to split into several files.\n\n4. Format and folder: in Settings → Reader / download path you choose where files are saved.\n\n5. After a download finishes, open it from Library / Downloads. Update re-downloads new chapters; Delete removes the local files but not your reading history.\n\nTip: slow sources work better with online reading. Translation options (when enabled) can make a download take longer.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_tts">Text to speech (TTS)</string>
    <string name="tutorial_tts_desc">How to listen to chapters with the voice reader</string>
    <string name="tutorial_tts_body">1. Open a chapter in the reader.\n\n2. Tap the speaker icon (bottom bar) to start reading aloud from the first visible sentence.\n\n3. While TTS is running, the TTS bar appears:\n• Play / Pause\n• Stop\n• Back / Forward (previous or next sentence)\n\n4. Open reader Settings (gear) → Voice tab to choose:\n• Language\n• Voice\n• Speed and pitch\n• Sleep timer (auto-stop)\n• Lock TTS scroll area (keeps the spoken line in view)\n\n5. You can also control Play / Pause / Stop from the notification while the screen is off.\n\nDefault voice:\n• QuickNovel prefers the free neural Piper voice “Dave” (es_ES-davefx-medium) for Spanish and “Lessac” for English when a Sherpa-ONNX / Piper TTS engine is installed.\n• Install Sherpa TTS Engine (Piper Dave ES) from the sherpa-onnx APKs, then open a chapter — the app picks that engine and voice automatically when available.\n\nTips:\n• If TTS fails, install language data for Android TTS (or Google Text-to-Speech).\n• Start from a clean paragraph; TTS begins at the first full sentence on screen.</string>
